Spec: Project/Instantiation

Purpose:
  Define HOW a concrete project instance gets produced from a raw
  customer prompt — the PROCESS, not the resulting content.

  CorePrinciple: PROJECT IS GENERATED, NOT PREDEFINED.

Pipeline:
  RAW PROMPT
    -> Prompt Analysis
    -> Skill Discovery
    -> Architecture Analysis
    -> Scale Analysis
    -> Complexity Analysis
    -> Dependency Analysis
    -> Project Decision (human approval)
    -> Project Instance (populate domains, modules, features, components)

  Each stage narrows what the next stage needs to consider.

ProjectScale:
  XS: trivial / single-purpose
  S: light modular application
  M: modular monolith
  L: strong modular architecture, partial independent scaling
  XL: distributed / service-oriented

  Scale drives how much of the hierarchy gets populated and which
  architecture patterns are eligible. Scale is a conclusion, not an input.

SkillFiltering:
  Project -> Relevant Skills -> Applicable Skills -> Required Skills -> Architecture

ArchitectureSelection:
  Customer Input -> Requirements -> Complexity -> Expected Growth
    -> Team/Operational Constraints -> Architecture Candidates
    -> Trade-off Analysis -> Recommended Architecture -> Human Approval

Evolution:
  Project instance MUST evolve as project evolves. Pipeline MUST be
  re-entered, scoped to the change, when new information invalidates
  an earlier stage's conclusion. MUST NOT discard already-confirmed
  information unless the change explicitly supersedes it.

Rules:
  [PI1] AI MUST classify ProjectScale from Complexity/Dependency analysis before proposing architecture.
  [PI2] AI MUST NOT apply a pattern solely because AI is familiar with it — every pattern proposal MUST trace back to analysis.
  [PI3] Files and entries MUST only be populated once analysis justifies them.
  [PI4] A recommended architecture MUST pass through Trade-off Analysis and MUST receive human approval.
  [PI5] Skill selection MUST follow Relevant -> Applicable -> Required narrowing.
  [PI6] This file MUST NOT redeclare the project hierarchy shape owned by project.sdd.
  [PI7] A project instance MUST evolve as the project evolves — pipeline MUST be re-entered, scoped to the change.
  [PI8] Evolution MUST NOT discard already-confirmed information unless the change explicitly supersedes it.
  [PI9] Human decisions at any pipeline gate MUST feed back into how AI generates and evaluates the project instance.

Navigation:
  Project hierarchy shape:        @./project.sdd
  Prompt intake:                  @../prompts/prompts.sdd
  Skill catalog:                  @../skills/skills.sdd
  Global architecture principles: @../architecture/principles.sdd
  This project's resolved arch.:  @./architecture.sdd
  Dependency graph:                @./dependencies.sdd
  Human decision gate:            @../PROJECT.sdd -> HumanDecision

State: +